---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Visual from '../components/Visual.astro';
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { sourceDirectory } from '../lib';
const tools=(await getCollection('tools')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Base>
<section class="hero section-shell"><div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE + COMMERCIAL LICENCE</div><h1>If you trade with CFD brokers,<br/><span>you’ll need these indicators.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">Exchange volume and company data on your CFD chart, browser improvements for TradingView, Trade Nation hotkeys and an independent trading history archive. Setup guides and source code included. Free for personal trading; a paid licence is required for company and work use.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/indicators/">Explore indicators <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="/userscripts/">Browse userscripts</a></div><div class="hero-facts"><span>Pine indicators</span><span>Browser userscripts</span><span><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m4 10 4 4 8-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg> Setup guides included</span></div></div><div class="hero-art"><div class="floating-chip"><span class="status-dot"></span> CFD CHART <span aria-hidden="true">↔</span> UNDERLYING MARKET</div><Visual kind="overview" capture="A CFD chart with Info, selected percentage levels and the mapped source visible."/><div class="hero-art-note"><span>01 / CFD CHART WITH MAPPED DATA</span><span>Illustrated workspace</span></div></div></section>
<div class="context-band"><div class="section-shell"><span>Company and earnings data.</span><span>Stock, futures and ETF volume.</span><span>Percentage levels on CFDs.</span><a href="/about/">Why these tools exist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
<section class="section-shell section-space" id="indicators"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / INDICATORS</div><h2>Company data, volume<br/>and CFD price levels.</h2></div><div><p>Match a CFD to its exchange or reference symbol, then show company information, selected volume or percentage levels on the chart. Built in Pine for TradingView.</p><a href="/indicators/" class="text-link">All indicators & setup <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><a class="setup-strip" href="/tools/symbol-mapper/"><div class="map-icon" aria-hidden="true">⇄</div><div><span class="mini-label">START HERE · SYMBOL MAPPER</span><h3>Share symbol mappings between indicators.</h3><p>Use shared mapping when your indicator needs it. Keep existing local maps and formulas when it does not.</p></div><span class="circle-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="tool-grid three">{tools.filter(t=>['info','real-volume','cfd-levels'].includes(t.id)).map(tool=><ToolCard tool={tool}/>)}</div></section>
<section class="browser-section section-space"><div class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / USERSCRIPTS</div><h2>Customise TradingView<br/>in your browser.</h2></div><div><p>Name your tabs, click recognised tickers, open saved AI questions for the current symbol and see watchlist prices on hover.</p><a href="/userscripts/tradingview/" class="text-link">TradingView userscripts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="browser-feature"><div><span class="outline-label">TRADINGVIEW WEBSITE · DESKTOP BROWSER</span><h3>See watchlist prices<br/>on hover.</h3><p>Keep the percentage in your watchlist. Hover to see a price. These enhancements run through a browser userscript manager, not inside TradingView Desktop.</p><a href="/tools/watchlist/" class="button secondary">Explore Watchlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-copy">Edge or Chrome + Tampermonkey is the current workflow.</p></div><Visual kind="watchlist" diagram="Example watchlist price interaction"/></div><div class="compact-links">{tools.filter(t=>t.data.group==='tradingview'&&t.id!=='watchlist').map(t=><a href={`/tools/${t.id}/`}><span>{t.data.label}</span><b>{t.data.name.replace('SVKO TradingView ','')} <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></b><p>{t.data.summary}</p></a>)}</div><div class="broker-teaser"><div><div class="eyebrow">ALSO IN USERSCRIPTS / TRADE NATION</div><h3>Trade Nation hotkeys.</h3></div><div><a href="/userscripts/trade-nation/">Trade Nation userscripts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section-shell section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT TOOL / TRADING STATISTICS</div><h2>Review your trading history.</h2><p>A local archive for results, costs and transactions. Currently imports Trade Nation CFD and Spread USD accounts. IG support is planned, not yet implemented.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/trading-statistics/">Explore Trading Statistics ↗</a></div></div><Visual kind="statistics" diagram="Collect, archive and review broker records"/></section>
<section class="section-shell section-space"><div class="open-source-panel" data-reveal><div class="source-glyph" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</div><div><div class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE + COMMERCIAL LICENCE</div><h2>Read the source.<br/>Report bugs or contribute.</h2><p>Read, use and modify the code free for personal use, including trading for your own profit. Company and work use require a paid commercial agreement. <a href="/licensing/">Read the terms and contact the author</a>. This is a source-available licence with business restrictions, not an OSI open-source licence.</p><a class="button primary" href={sourceDirectory}>Source code <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="source-details"><span>Public source</span><span>Practical documentation</span><span>Issues & pull requests</span><a href="/licensing/">Licences and attribution ↗</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
